---
import BaseHead from '../../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title="BenchmarkKit | Ravikumar Buragapu"
			description="BenchmarkKit compares LLM inference servers and RAG pipelines on latency, throughput, cost, retrieval recall, and answer support."
		/>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<p>OPEN-SOURCE TOOLKIT · PYTHON · DOCKER</p>
			<h1>BenchmarkKit</h1>
			<p>
				Make LLM serving and RAG trade-offs measurable. BenchmarkKit
				runs repeatable workloads against OpenAI-compatible endpoints
				and evaluates retrieval and generation results with transparent,
				documented metrics.
			</p>

			<section aria-labelledby="inference">
				<h2 id="inference">Inference, under load</h2>
				<p>
					Compare vLLM, TGI, SGLang, and TensorRT-LLM using
					throughput, P50/P95/P99 latency, streaming TTFT,
					token throughput, and estimated cost per 1,000 tokens.
					Export run metrics to Prometheus and inspect JSON results
					in the Streamlit dashboard.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section aria-labelledby="rag">
				<h2 id="rag">RAG, with evidence</h2>
				<p>
					Measure recall@k against labeled relevant documents,
					end-to-end latency, and a deterministic answer-term
					support proxy. The proxy is clearly distinguished from
					semantic faithfulness or an LLM-judge evaluation.
				</p>
				<p>
					Bring JSONL records transformed from public datasets such
					as HotpotQA or Natural Questions, with dataset versions
					and licenses documented for each experiment.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section aria-labelledby="start">
				<h2 id="start">Start a reproducible run</h2>
				<pre><code>pip install -e ".[dashboard]"
benchmarkkit inference \
  --dataset samples/prompts.jsonl \
  --endpoint http://localhost:8000/v1/chat/completions \
  --model your-served-model --framework vllm</code></pre>
				<p>
					The toolkit includes Docker Compose for the results
					dashboard and Prometheus, sample JSONL fixtures, metric
					assumptions, and contributor guidance.
				</p>
				<p><a href="/">Back to profile</a></p>
			</section>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
